 the first course in a sequence specially crafted for adults seeking the most direct path to prepare for university math courses. The course starts with fraction arithmetic and covers all the way up through the algebra of linear equations. Upon completing the course, students will be prepared for Mathematical Foundations II, the second step of the journey towards university-level math." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1009 "Solidify your arithmetic, learn about variables and graphs, level up your algebra, and learn the essentials of geometry." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1012 113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1013 "MF1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1014 #uuid "042e624c-a46d-509f-a48e-61bd6d3e082c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1031 "Multiplying Fractions Using Models" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1033 3079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048962 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "cfc8bab9-3c84-588c-af07-f2c8e11b8d36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1031 "Multiplying Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1033 2378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049253 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "e6d4682e-e5ec-5a7f-a918-a708b14b5010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1031 "Multiplying Fractions by Unit Fractions Using Models" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1033 565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050954 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "75482856-dc6f-5409-9718-62a9c17846a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161716 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161716 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/01/0144d5fb5264162b7b2f03f71469f261c33c813ee235743c9e631edd7d4d049c.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161716 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "432754ac-d9f0-5843-a751-b13821e2e725" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161716 #edb/ref 1074 "We have $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{6}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/f0/f087c076a86b5bab709af23db87d63ed66363d4d580c23dc453573f264fb28bc.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{6}{20}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161717 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14523" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161717 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/23/23940bc011c6cd71c0d9d58b4bab0b175722a21fd1c80062ed5cb5ceff3729c0.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the multiplication problem above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161717 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1fbd22af-5d6d-58ff-ac16-cfbb1d2577de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161717 #edb/ref 1074 "We have $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{9}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/31/31badccda3cc3548e2bdc40158e88d32feddcf92b8fdd4d4ae18f08396ca8cfc.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $5$ equal parts by horizontal lines.\nSo, the shaded part on the right is $\\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5}$ of the shaded part on the left. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4} \\times \\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5} = \\dfrac{9}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161718 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14528" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161718 #edb/ref 1071 "What picture is missing from the multiplication model below?\n\n![](images/0d/0d381d096814ced0d6637ce373e14d77f317e1d8f202ed75371f744804d99f3c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161718 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "493da564-eed4-5ec7-b527-63fd3a68fc95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161718 #edb/ref 1074 "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{\\color{red}4}{\\color{blue}5}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}4$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](images/97/978789f7aed1ea0e0dc8794aaeb00a3829168101e792129e72c0585fac43ebe2.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{8}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](images/fa/faf527aba9974aa23b9a5bffd8fc8f54a2135fce10bf2d09a7133556ab4b95e3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161719 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14539" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161719 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/60/6026c90a1101bf484ab649dcb35964ae4b136fc7784e384d1cf5d90ea47a96a2.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{2}{6} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161719 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e14de76-f6e2-51f8-9590-8283fe81ce82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161719 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}4}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}3$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](images/0f/0f7c5ff7155c00a811c744606ee039e764c6ded16f214a163b6d5d4a481e633b.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{6}{24}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{6}{24}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying a Multiplication Problem Corresponding to a Model" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186161716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161913 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3443d2b1-14c5-50ba-90b3-73b8bef47016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161914 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161914 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161914 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161914 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161914 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying